.Dd @MDOCDATE@
.Dt CLOWN-CATALOG 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm clown-catalog
.Nd what a capability profile names: the catalog an enforcer presents, for profile writers
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A capability profile
.Pq Li \&! espalier-profile-v1
admits an agent session's tool calls by matching the subjects an enforcer
presents for each call: a path of catalog nodes (plugin, server, tool) and,
under the tool, one instance subject per input.
This page is for the writer of such a profile.
It answers the three questions profile writers get wrong most often:
.Bl -enum -offset indent
.It
where the harness built-ins hang
.Pq Sx THE HARNESS BUILT-INS ;
.It
which input fields are paths or tree references rather than plain values
.Pq Sx FIELD KINDS ;
.It
how a lock is spelled and where its digest comes from
.Pq Sx LOCKS .
.El
.Pp
clown RFC 0018 (the capability catalog contract,
.Pa docs/rfcs/0018-capability-catalog-contract.md )
is normative; where this page and the RFC disagree, the RFC is right.
The rules a profile body must also follow are RFC 0019's; the matching is
cutting-garden's
.Xr ajour 7 .
.Sh THE CATALOG PATH
Every call is presented under three catalog nodes, always in this order:
.Bl -tag -width "mcp-server-v1"
.It Li clown-plugin-v1
the clown plugin name, verbatim:
.Li moxy ,
.Li just-us ,
.Li cutting-garden ,
.Li spinclass ,
.Li clown-builtin-jobs ,
.Li clown-builtin-harness .
.It Li mcp-server-v1
the MCP server inside the plugin.
For moxy this is the child server
.Pq Li folio , Li rg , Li grit , Li smith , No ... ,
and
.Li moxy
for moxy's own tools and resources.
.It Li mcp-tool-v1
the tool name as its server spells it, verbatim:
.Li read ,
.Li issue-list ,
.Li run_recipe ,
.Li Read .
.El
.Pp
Ids are never normalized: no case folding, no
.Ql _
for
.Ql - .
The harness's prefixed spelling
.Pq Li mcp__plugin_moxy_moxy__folio_read
is never an id, and neither is its
.Li folio_read :
moxy names that tool
.Li folio.read ,
and the server is the text before the first
.Ql \&. ,
so it is
.Li moxy
/
.Li folio
/
.Li read .
A moxy tool with no
.Ql \&.
in its name
.Pq Li status , Li async
is under server
.Li moxy .
RFC 0019 warns on a
.Ql _ Ns -joined
moxy id (W-5).
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[moxy !clown-plugin-v1
  [-> folio !mcp-server-v1
    [-> read !mcp-tool-v1 [-> file:eng/repos !fs-path-v1 subtree]]]]
.Ed
.Sh THE HARNESS BUILT-INS
The tools the harness implements itself (claude-code's
.Li Read ,
.Li Edit ,
.Li Write ,
.Li NotebookEdit ,
.Li Glob ,
.Li Grep ,
.Li Bash ,
.Li Agent ,
.Li Skill ,
.Li WebFetch ,
.Li WebSearch )
hang under a plugin and server clown declares for them:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[clown-builtin-harness !clown-plugin-v1
  [-> harness !mcp-server-v1
    [-> Read !mcp-tool-v1 [-> file:eng/repos !fs-path-v1 subtree]]
    [-> Edit !mcp-tool-v1 [-> file:eng/repos/x/.worktrees/w !fs-path-v1 subtree]]]]
.Ed
.Pp
Two exceptions:
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Li ReadMcpResourceTool
and
.Li ListMcpResourcesTool
present no tool step.
The call is presented as the resource read it is, under the server that
owns the URI's scheme
.Pq Sx RESOURCES .
A node for either tool under
.Li clown-builtin-harness/harness
never matches anything (RFC 0019 warns, W-2).
.It
.Li Bash
.Pq and moxy's Li toolbox/run
take one opaque
.Li command
value.
A profile that admits either with the command open admits every file and
host the command line can name; the catalog cannot scope it (RFC 0019
warns, W-1).
.El
.Sh FIELD KINDS
Each input field of a tool is presented as exactly one kind.
The kind decides what a profile writes under the tool:
.Bl -tag -width "reference"
.It path
one
.Li fs-path-v1
subject per path, with
.Li field= Ns Ar name
and no verb (the tool is the verb).
Write
.Li [-> file: Ns Ar id Li !fs-path-v1 subtree] .
.It reference
one resource path per object, under the surface of the server that owns the
URI's scheme
.Pq Sx RESOURCES ,
never under the tool.
.It content
a value that is, whole, a
.Li madder://blobs/ Ns Ar digest
URI is a resource read under
.Li moxy/moxy ;
any other value is an input.
.It recipe
.Li run_recipe Ns 's
recipe and its arguments, as a value path under the tool.
.It route
nothing: the enforcer consumes it.
.It input
the default: one
.Li tool-input-v1
subject,
.Li field= Ns Ar name Li value= Ns Ar value .
Write
.Li [-> _ !tool-input-v1 field=repo value=[a, b]]
beside
.Li [-> _ !tool-input-v1 ^field=repo open] .
.El
.Pp
The path and reference fields of the tools a writer meets most:
.Bl -column "cutting-garden list_nodes, read_node, read_facets" "source, destination" -offset indent
.It Sy tool Ta Sy path fields Ta Sy reference fields
.It harness Read, Edit, Write Ta file_path Ta \(em
.It harness NotebookEdit Ta notebook_path Ta \(em
.It harness Glob, Grep Ta path Ta \(em
.It harness ReadMcpResourceTool Ta \(em Ta uri
.It moxy folio read, write Ta file_path Ta \(em
.It moxy folio ls, glob, tree, mkdir, chmod, ... Ta path Ta \(em
.It moxy folio rm Ta paths Ta \(em
.It moxy folio cp, mv Ta source, destination Ta \(em
.It moxy folio link Ta source, target Ta \(em
.It moxy rg search Ta path Ta \(em
.It moxy jq jq Ta files, cwd Ta \(em
.It moxy grit status, diff, log Ta paths Ta \(em
.It moxy grit commit, merge, remote, tag Ta repo_path Ta \(em
.It moxy grit branch, stage, stash Ta repo_path, paths Ta \(em
.It moxy grit clone Ta source, destination Ta \(em
.It moxy chix build, flake-* Ta flake_dir Ta \(em
.It spinclass grit_* Ta repo_path (and as grit) Ta \(em
.It cutting-garden list_nodes, read_node, read_facets Ta \(em Ta uri
.It cutting-garden mutate_nodes Ta \(em Ta groups
.It moxy chrest, nebulous resource-read Ta \(em Ta uri
.El
.Pp
The
.Li stdin
of moxy's
.Li jq
and
.Li toolbox run
is content.
.Pp
The complete table is
.Pa internal/*/catalogcontract/catalog.json ;
the live listing
.Pq Sx THE LIVE LISTING
shows each field's kind as its
.Li field_kind
facet.
A field neither lists is an input.
.Ss Spelling a path
A path is presented by its canonical
.Li file:
id: symlinks resolved, no
.Ql \&.
or
.Ql .. ,
no trailing slash.
Under the home directory it is
.Li file:
and the path relative to home, with no leading
.Ql / :
.Li file:eng/repos/clown/.worktrees/w .
Elsewhere it is
.Li file:
and the absolute path:
.Li file:/nix/store .
A worktree reached through a symlink is presented by its resolved path,
so a profile naming the symlink never matches.
.Pp
A path field holding a URI with another scheme
.Pq Li madder:// , Li clown://
is a resource read under that scheme's owner, not a path.
A glob pattern that is absolute or has a
.Ql ..
segment is refused before the profile is asked.
.Sh RESOURCES
A server's resources hang under one surface node beside its tools,
.Li [-> resources !mcp-resources-v1] ,
and every resource step carries its verb as
.Li op=
.Pq Li read , Li patch , Li put , Li delete .
The owning server is chosen by the URI's scheme:
.Li madder:
is
.Li moxy/moxy ;
.Li chrest:
and
.Li nebulous:
are their moxy servers;
.Li clown:
is
.Li clown-builtin-diagnostics/disconnects ;
cutting-garden's schemes
.Pq Li caldav: , Li org: , Li smith: , No ...
are
.Li cutting-garden/cutting-garden .
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[moxy !clown-plugin-v1 [-> moxy !mcp-server-v1
  [-> resources !mcp-resources-v1
    [-> madder://blobs !mcp-resource-v1 subtree op=[read]]]]]
.Ed
.Sh PERM AND PATCHES
A
.Li perm=
atom is the profile's decision for the calls that reach that node, not a
copy of the manifest's tier, and it never has to match anything:
.Bl -tag -width "dynamic"
.It Li allow
the enforcer skips its own ask prompt for the call;
.It Li ask
the call is admitted subject to a human: an attended session prompts, an
unattended one escalates when it has a channel and otherwise refuses;
.It Li dynamic
the same as no
.Li perm
atom: the manifest's tier decides.
.El
.Pp
It may sit on any node, not only a tool node: one
.Li perm
per node, written
.Li perm= Ns Ar value
with one value, never negated and never beside
.Li deny
(RFC 0019 R-14).
Because it matches nothing, a typed
.Li _
node whose only atom is
.Li perm
is still a wildcard and needs
.Li open
(R-4).
.Pp
A patch only denies: every leaf carries
.Li deny ,
and a patch carries no
.Li perm .
Whether a patch may ask is awaiting a ruling.
.Pp
.Li kind ,
unlike
.Li perm ,
is a fact that must match.
No moxy tool presents one yet, so
.Li [-> _ !mcp-tool-v1 kind=read ...]
admits no moxy call: name each moxy tool instead (RFC 0019 W-6).
.Sh LOCKS
A lock pins a tool to the exact input schema the writer reviewed: the
tool's id is followed by
.Ql @
and the schema's digest.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[-> run_recipe@blake2b256-<digest> !mcp-tool-v1]
.Ed
.Pp
The digest is the blake2b256 markl id
.Pq Xr markl-id 7
of the canonical JSON (sorted keys, no whitespace) of the tool's MCP
.Li inputSchema .
A server that changes the tool's schema changes the digest, and the locked
node stops matching until the profile is re-locked.
Never compute a digest by hand, and never use a digest of anything else:
an enforcer that cannot present the same digest refuses every lock beneath
it.
Copy the digest from the live listing: reading a tool node gives its
.Li lock .
The harness built-ins have no schema and cannot be locked.
.Sh THE LIVE LISTING
Every clown launch records what its servers report, and
.Ic clown catalog traversal-serve ,
a cutting-garden traversal plugin, serves the running sessions as
.Li clown-catalog:// Ns Ar principal Ns Li / Ns Ar plugin Ns Li / Ns Ar server Ns Li / Ns Ar tool Ns Li / Ns Ar input :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
cg list -format espalier clown-catalog://<principal>/moxy/folio
.Ed
.Pp
A tool node carries its
.Li kind
and
.Li perm
facets when known (the
.Li perm
facet is the manifest's tier, shown for reference; see
.Sx PERM AND PATCHES ) ;
reading it
.Pq Li read_node
gives those and its
.Li lock .
An input node's
.Li field_kind
facet is its kind
.Pq Sx FIELD KINDS .
The listing copies ids, digests and kinds exactly as an enforcer will
present them, so a writer copies from it rather than guessing.
.Pp
The listing is only as complete as the launch that recorded it: servers
started inside an agent unit are absent, a harness built-in lists only the
inputs the contract names (its full parameter list is the harness's, not
readable by clown), and a moxy older than moxy#517 has its server, tool and
.Li perm
read from its advertised names and descriptions instead of its metadata
(RFC 0018 \(sc9 item 7).
No moxy tool presents a
.Li kind
yet, so
.Li [-> _ !mcp-tool-v1 kind=read ...]
admits no moxy call: name each moxy tool instead (RFC 0019 W-6).
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr clown 1 ,
.Xr cutting-garden 1 ,
.Xr ajour 7 ,
.Xr markl-id 7 ,
.Xr moxin 7
.Pp
clown RFC 0018 (the catalog contract) and RFC 0019 (the profile rules);
cutting-garden FDR 0028 (ajour).
